+# FlyWeb: release after 3.2.2 (softmac `seguridad/siguiente-3`), V8 fix d76136bcef (crbug 589433702), ported from the M159 merge
+
+SEGURIDAD-PORTES-33, 25-11-2026 (softmac `FlyWeb/seguridad/siguiente-3/brave-core/0008`). **Not merged to 15.6
+upstream yet**: ported from the M159 merge d76136bcef (V8 15.9.128.39, bugs 590348412 and 589433702; cherry-pick of
+main eb88dd314f). Applied as is to 15.6.75.66 (`runtime-scopes.cc` already had a FlyWeb patch; no conflict). Severity
+not published.
+
+- In `DebugEvaluate::Local` (DevTools "evaluate on call frame"), a `var`/`function` declared by the snippet was hoisted
+  past the synthetic `DebugEvaluateContext` without the parser's conflict check. `DeclareEvalHelper` could then write a
+  module cell index into a `ModuleContext` (or cast a `SourceTextModule` to `JSObject`), overwrite `const`/`let`
+  slots or wrap TDZ slots: memory corruption.
+- Now any `ModuleContext` is rejected up front with `EvalError` (`kVarNotAllowedInEvalScope`), and lexical, read-only
+  or non-simple-parameter `arguments` bindings throw a `SyntaxError` redeclaration error. New `DCHECK`s only.
+- Reachable only through the debugger (DevTools open, or an extension with the `debugger` permission); applies to Mac.
+
+**Cache epoch:** covered by the single 40 -> 41 bump of `siguiente-3` (`brave-core/0001`); no bytecode change.
+
+To check (D8-LINUX): inspector test `debugger/evaluate-on-call-frame-redeclaration` and `inspector/debugger/*`.
+
 # FlyWeb: release after 3.2.2 (softmac `seguridad/siguiente-3`), V8 fix 474a6307ce (crbug 576333024), M156 reland
 
